The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
reg = mcp251x_read_reg(spi, CANSTAT);
if ((reg & CANCTRL_REQOP_MASK) != CANCTRL_REQOP_CONF)
```
Reason:
The original implementation checks the status of the MCP251x device immediately after a reset, assuming it will enter configuration mode within 5ms. If the device takes longer to stabilize, this check can return an error prematurely, even though the device is still powering up correctly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
timeout = jiffies + HZ;
while ((mcp251x_read_reg(spi, CANSTAT) & CANCTRL_REQOP_MASK) !=
       CANCTRL_REQOP_CONF) {
    usleep_range(MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS * 1000,
                 MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS * 1000 * 2);
    if (time_after(jiffies, timeout)) {
        dev_err(&spi->dev,
            "MCP251x didn't enter in conf mode after reset\n");
        return -EBUSY;
    }
}
```
Reason:
The patch introduces a loop that repeatedly checks the device status until it enters configuration mode or a timeout occurs. This allows for additional time for the device to stabilize after a reset, preventing premature failure detection and ensuring proper communication with the device.

